asteroid is a modified version of ryoshot from Ryoku
(https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku, commit e344edb), licensed GPL-3.0.
asteroid is distributed under the same license (see LICENSE).

Modifications (GPL-3.0 section 5), relative to upstream ryoshot:

- Renamed ryoshot to asteroid: config name, IPC target, layer namespace,
  lock/trigger/temp files, environment variables, notification app name, and
  settings paths (now ~/.config/asteroid/).
- Removed the dependency on Ryoku.Ui.Singletons. Added local singletons in
  quickshell/Singletons/: Tokens (colours from the Caelestia scheme at
  ~/.local/state/caelestia/scheme.json, with the upstream values as fallback),
  I18n (English passthrough), Spawn, and Wm (Hyprland-only, via hyprctl).
- Removed Ryoku-only features and all network access: OCR, reverse image search,
  upload to a file host, recording (including key press and webcam toggles),
  pin to desktop, shutter sound, the hotkey rebind row and the link to the Ryoku
  hub in the settings panel, and the Ryoku brand file.
- Replaced ryoku-cmd-grim and ryoku-shell clip-copy with grim and wl-copy.
- Added freeze-on-press: the launcher grabs every output with grim at key press
  and Overlay.qml loads those files (ASTEROID_PRECAPTURED).
- Added standby mode: bin/asteroid-standby keeps one pre-started instance
  (ASTEROID_STANDBY) that opens through a watched trigger file or IPC.
  The standby script resolves WAYLAND_DISPLAY from hyprctl and backs off if the
  instance dies at once.
- Replaced the launcher with bin/asteroid; added install.sh.
- Dropped the node-based *.test.mjs files for lib/*.js.
